### ✅ **PL/SQL Part**

#### **C. Write a PL/SQL Block to Generate the Fibonacci Series**

Here’s a PL/SQL block that generates the Fibonacci series up to a given limit.

```sql
DECLARE
    num1 NUMBER := 0;
    num2 NUMBER := 1;
    next_num NUMBER;
    limit NUMBER := 10; -- Change this limit as needed
BEGIN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Fibonacci Series:');
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(num1);
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(num2);
    
    FOR i IN 3..limit LOOP
        next_num := num1 + num2;
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(next_num);
        num1 := num2;
        num2 := next_num;
    END LOOP;
END;
```

This PL/SQL block prints the Fibonacci series up to the specified `limit` (in this case, 10).

